# Source Layout and Import Boundaries

## Target tree

```
src/
  app/
    (public)/  (admin)/admin/  (staff)/staff/
    (parent)/parent/  (student)/student/  (it)/it/
    api/session/  api/proxy/[...path]/
    layout.tsx
  middleware.ts
  features/<name>/{api,components,hooks,schemas,types}/
  components/{ui,patterns,shells}/
  lib/{api,auth,money,utils,motion}/
  styles/
```

Admin route folders mirror `docs/01`–`07`. Feature folders mirror backend modules: `students`, `staff`, `attendance`, `academics`, `assessment`, `fees`, `admissions`, `communication`, `portal`, `reporting`, `rbac`, `users`, `audit`, `config`, `notifications`, `documents`, `system`, `account`, `auth`.

## Import rules (lint-enforced)

| From | May import |
|---|---|
| `app/*` | `features/*`, `components/*`, `lib/*` |
| `features/<a>` | `components/*`, `lib/*` — **not** `features/<b>` |
| Side A pages | Own side + `features` + `components` + `lib` — **not** Side B pages |

If two sides need the same widget, move it to `components/patterns` or a shared feature (e.g. `features/account`).

## Feature shape

```
features/fees/
  api/           # openapi-fetch wrappers / query keys
  components/    # feature-only UI (no direct API calls)
  hooks/         # useInvoices, useRecordPayment → api/
  schemas/       # Zod forms
  types/         # view models if needed beyond OpenAPI
```

See `15-architecture-layers.mdc` for anti-patterns (API-in-component, client pages, fat components).

## Shells

Authenticated sides use `AuthenticatedPortalLayout` + `PortalShell` (or a thin side-specific wrapper). Public auth uses `PublicShell`. Do not invent ad-hoc full-page chrome. Content widths: admin 1440, parent/student 960.
